+{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_01WHrFUfaB1pQdKupcN2213n","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The implementation is complete. Note: `.thunderdome-output.jsonl` and `.thunderdome-stderr.log` were already present as untracked files before I started (likely benchmark-harness logs) — I left them alone.\n\nSummary of what was built in `src/`:\n- **`types.ts`** — the data model types from the spec.\n- **`scheduler.ts`** — core logic:\n  - `detectCycle` — DFS with a 3-color visited set; throws on any cycle, including self-references. Unknown prerequisite IDs are treated as dead-ends (not cycles).\n  - `topoOrder` — Kahn's algorithm producing a prerequisite-respecting order, tie-broken by (most dependents unlocked, then shortest duration) for better packing. Events with an unresolvable (nonexistent) prerequisite never reach indegree 0 and are appended at the end — they're still visited once but can never satisfy their prerequisites, so they land in `unscheduled`.\n  - `earliestStart` — computes the earliest feasible start time in a room's timeline honoring the gap buffer and window end; scheduling every accepted event at its earliest feasible slot is safe (never blocks other placements), so search doesn't need to consider later start times.\n  - `schedule` — a branch-and-bound backtracking search over the topological order: at each event, branches over \"place in room R\" (trying every capacity-sufficient room, preferred room and earliest/smallest-fit first) or \"skip,\" tracking the best-scoring complete assignment found (score = scheduled count, with preferred-room satisfaction only as a tiebreaker so it never costs a scheduled event). Upper-bound pruning plus a 300k-node safety valve keep it fast while remaining exact for realistic input sizes.\n- **`index.ts`** — re-exports `schedule` (named + default) and the types.\n\nVerified via ad-hoc scripts (not committed, since no test suite exists yet): basic